  "id": "COMPOUND:42136 - PROTEIN:6324",
  "verbalization": "Neoclovene is implicated in the regulation of M-phase phosphoprotein 8 through a series of target relationships that involve the MIP family of compounds. The evidence suggests that Neoclovene acts as a target for multiple compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, Camelliquercetiside B, and Tetraethylammonium, all of which are known to interact with M-phase phosphoprotein 8. These findings indicate that Neoclovene may exert its biological effects by modulating the activity of these compounds, which in turn influence the phosphorylation of M-phase phosphoprotein 8. The consistent presence of these targets across different pathways supports a mechanism where Neoclovene indirectly affects M-phase phosphoprotein 8 through its interaction with these compounds. The integration of these relationships highlights a potential regulatory network involving the MIP family and the M-phase phosphoprotein 8, suggesting that Neoclovene may play a role in the cellular processes associated with the M-phase of the cell cycle.",
